  "notes": "Sheet 0 (Guillaume Ramillien, the Le Cèdre socio-cultural centre in the Hauts d'Asnières district, Hauts-de-Seine, 2010s): a prefabricated timber building of spruce and Douglas fir in posts and beams, white brick cladding and zinc roofs, built round three gardens and the district's preserved cedars. From the street: a tall gabled volume of white brick with one slot window (photographs 1 and 4), then a long low wing of vertical timber piers and glass under a zinc roof with a deep timber-soffit eave (photographs 1 and 6), and behind it a three-storey timber building of fine vertical members and full glazing with a shallow zinc mono-pitch, the big cedar of Lebanon in the court between them (photographs 2 and 3). Modelled: the three volumes with their roofs and glazing, the street and pavement, the cedar, the gravel garden, the play lawn and vegetable beds. Guessed: every dimension (a 30 m three-storey block), the court's shape. A public building placed at its department only (Hauts-de-Seine; the article does not give its address)"
